// Enemies along the path. Durations in ticks (60/s), distances in metres, as in boss.ron.
// Attacks use the same format as the boss's (minus `phases`).
//
// - sight: detection distance (in front of it if it's watching; half as far, but all around,
//   if it's asleep). leash: it gives up if it strays too far from its post, goes back and heals.
// - poise: damage taken within ~1 s before being staggered (0 = every hit staggers it).
// - scale / tint: a type can reuse another's model, scaled up and tinted; its hit
//   capsules must then be given at that scale. Animations are retimed to the
//   hit windows as long as the number of hits of each attack doesn't change.
// - loot: what it may drop when its body vanishes (at most one item; each `chance` is out of
//   1, their sum at most 1). Temporary boosts only: the game is about skill, there's no levelling.
(
    kinds: [
        (
            key: "hound", model: "hound", scale: 1.3,
            name: (en: "Stray Hound", fr: "Chien errant"),
            max_hp: 120, radius: 0.55, height: 1.17, mass: 0.9,
            walk_speed: 1.8, run_speed: 6.0, turn_rate: 480,
            sight: 11, leash: 24, preferred_range: 2.3, idle_ticks: (14, 46),
            poise: 0,
